<title>UK: Polska Telefonia unit sets $253 mln 10 year bond. [CORRECTED 23:17 GMT]</title>
<headline>Polska Telefonia unit sets $253 mln 10 year bond. [CORRECTED 23:17 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following discount bond was announced by lead manager Salomon Brothers.</p>
<p> BORROWER   PTC INTERNATIONAL FINANCE B.V.</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  POLSKA TELEFONIA CYFROWA</p>
<p> AMT    $253 MLN	COUPON    *ZERO	MATURITY    01.JUL.07</p>
<p> TYPE	 STEP-UP   ISS PRICE  59.241    PAY DATE    01.JUL.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.0645    REOFFER    59.241    SPREAD	+434 BP</p>
<p> NOTES     *FOR FIRST FIVE-YEARS THEN STEPS-UP TO 10.75 PCT</p>
<p>		THEREAFTER.</p>
<p> MOODY	B3	  GOV LAW    NEW YORK</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.5645    SELL CONC  0.50</p>
<p> NOTES	UNSECURED SENIOR SUBORDINASTED GUARANTEED DISCOUNT</p>
<p>		NOTES.</p>
<p>(Lead manager corrects issue and reoffer price from 59.201 to 59.241.)</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
